      "output": {
        "question": "what is the sumary of the first book?",
        "answer": "The provided search results do not contain a comprehensive summary of the first book, *The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo*. The available passages only offer fragmented details: Mikael Blomkvist was imprisoned for libeling Hans-Erik Wennerström [E1]; he was hired by Henrik Vanger to investigate Harriet Vanger's disappearance [E2]; Lisbeth Salander was involved in the investigation [E2]; Martin Vanger was identified as a killer [E3]; and Harriet Vanger had fled [E4]. However, the specific resolution of the mystery (Harriet's fate, Martin's death) and Blomkvist's vindication are not fully detailed in the cited snippets to form a complete summary.\n\nTherefore, I cannot provide a full summary based solely on the provided evidence.",
        "citations": [
          "[E1]",
          "[E2]",
          "[E3]",
          "[E4]"
        ],
        "reranked": [
          {
            "book": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo",
            "book_file": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo -- Larsson, Stieg -- Millennium book, 1st Vintage Crime_Black Lizard mass-market -- Random House, Incorporated -- isbn13 9780307455352 -- f10e68d0e06407c85b6ba58f6f49d618 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "The_Girl_with_the_Dragon_Tattoo_split_008.html",
            "paragraph": 18,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": "CHAPTER 1 Friday, December 20",
            "page": "7",
            "text": "“Three months in gaol and 150,000 kronor damages. That’s pretty severe,” said She from TV4.\n“I’ll survive.”\n“Are you going to apologise to Wennerström? Shake his hand?”\n“I think not.”\n“So you still would say that he’s a crook?” Dagens Nyheter .\nThe court had just ruled that Blomkvist had libelled and defamed the financier Hans-Erik Wennerström. The trial was over and he had no plans to appeal. So what would happen if he repeated his claim on the courthouse steps? Blomkvist decided that he did not want to find out.",
            "paragraph_end": 23,
            "part_end": 1,
            "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1",
            "source_id": "6067d833af95b35377a3ea1d49a28e4f92c57898c20afbbdf7f4a68ba5079aa6",
            "id": "6067d833-af95-b353-77a3-ea1d49a28e4f",
            "score": 4.480276107788086,
            "agent_label": "E1"
          },
          {
            "book": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo",
            "book_file": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo -- Larsson, Stieg -- Millennium book, 1st Vintage Crime_Black Lizard mass-market -- Random House, Incorporated -- isbn13 9780307455352 -- f10e68d0e06407c85b6ba58f6f49d618 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "The_Girl_with_the_Dragon_Tattoo_split_022.html",
            "paragraph": 169,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": "CHAPTER 14 Saturday, March 8– Monday, March 17",
            "page": "21",
            "text": "The lawyer Frode from Hedestad had hired her to do an investigation of Mikael Blomkvist, the journalist who was given a prison sentence for libelling financier Hans-Erik Wennerström. A few months later Henrik Vanger, also from Hedestad, joins Blomkvist’s magazine’s board of directors and claims that there is a conspiracy to crush the magazine. All this on the same day that the former goes to prison. Most fascinating of all: a two-year-old background article—“With two empty hands”—about Hans-Erik Wennerström, which she found in the online edition of Monopoly Financial Magazine . It seemed that he began his career in the very same Vanger Corporation in the late sixties.\nYou didn’t have to be a rocket scientist to see that these events were somehow related. There had to be a skeleton in one of their cupboards, and Salander loved hunting skeletons. Besides, she had nothing else on at the moment.",
            "paragraph_end": 170,
            "part_end": 1,
            "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1",
            "source_id": "46b8b531008f65b4d8a0107059592ecfb13b3277c185b633339e5375ef3e8968",
            "id": "46b8b531-008f-65b4-d8a0-107059592ecf",
            "score": 4.08872652053833,
            "agent_label": "E2"
          },
          {
            "book": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo",
            "book_file": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo -- Larsson, Stieg -- Millennium book, 1st Vintage Crime_Black Lizard mass-market -- Random House, Incorporated -- isbn13 9780307455352 -- f10e68d0e06407c85b6ba58f6f49d618 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "The_Girl_with_the_Dragon_Tattoo_split_035.html",
            "paragraph": 5,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": "CHAPTER 25 Saturday, July 12– Monday, July 14",
            "page": "34",
            "text": "Together with Mikael Blomkvist she had taken up the hunt for what they thought was a serial killer from the past. They had found something appallingly different. She could hardly imagine the horrors that must have played out in Martin Vanger’s basement, in the midst of this well-ordered, idyllic spot.\nShe tried to understand.\nMartin Vanger had been killing women since the sixties, during the past fifteen years one or two victims per year. The killing had been done so discreetly and was so well planned that no-one was even aware that a serial killer was at work. How was that possible?",
            "paragraph_end": 7,
            "part_end": 1,
            "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1",
            "source_id": "893923af170055c906d98d59f8cc20ba075581d6e51e09dffdb2bc0fbea3d4a9",
            "id": "893923af-1700-55c9-06d9-8d59f8cc20ba",
            "score": 5.479121208190918,
            "agent_label": "E3"
          },
          {
            "book": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo",
            "book_file": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo -- Larsson, Stieg -- Millennium book, 1st Vintage Crime_Black Lizard mass-market -- Random House, Incorporated -- isbn13 9780307455352 -- f10e68d0e06407c85b6ba58f6f49d618 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "The_Girl_with_the_Dragon_Tattoo_split_037.html",
            "paragraph": 11,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": "CHAPTER 27 Saturday, July 26– Monday, July 28",
            "page": "36",
            "text": "“Bitch,” she said.\n“Who?”\n“Harriet Fucking Vanger. If she had done something in 1966, Martin Vanger couldn’t have kept killing and raping for thirty-seven years.”\n“Harriet knew about her father murdering women, but she had no idea that Martin had anything to do with it. She fled from a brother who raped her and then threatened to reveal that she had drowned her father if she didn’t do what he said.”",
