              "answer": "The first book, *The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo*, follows journalist Mikael Blomkvist, who is imprisoned for libeling financier Hans-Erik Wennerström. To clear his name, he accepts a secret assignment from Henrik Vanger to investigate the 40-year-old disappearance of his niece, Harriet Vanger. Blomkvist is assisted by Lisbeth Salander, a brilliant hacker and investigator. Together they discover that Martin Vanger was a serial killer who murdered young women in Harriet's image. Harriet had actually fled the island after discovering her father's crimes and Martin's activities; she later confirms to Blomkvist that Martin died in a car accident (likely suicide). The book ends with Blomkvist publishing an exposé on Wennerström, vindicating himself, and forming a close bond with Salander.",
